<title>SOUTH KOREA: Ssangyong wins $180 mln Singapore racetrack order.</title>
<headline>Ssangyong wins $180 mln Singapore racetrack order.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Ssangyong Engineering and Construction Co Ltd, an unlisted unit of Ssangyong Group, said on Thursday it won a $180 million order to build a horse track in Singapore.  </p>
<p>Ssangyong said in a statement that the order was awarded by the Singapore Turf Club.</p>
<p>Construction of the course, which will start on Thursday in Kranji, north Singapore, was expected to take 24 months to complete, it said.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5643</p>
</text>
